response:
 To write a C++ program for the bubble sort algorithm using minimal memory and avoiding potential errors, follow these steps:
1. Define a function to swap elements in the array:
```cpp
void swap(int* a, int* b) {
    int temp = *a;
    *a = *b;
    *b = temp;
}
```
2. Write the bubble sort function:
```cpp
void bubbleSort(int arr[], int n) {
    for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
        for (int j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++) {
            if (arr[j] > arr[j + 1]) {
                swap(&arr[j], &arr[j + 1]);
            }
        }
    }
}
```
